
                                                    MDG1TPORT CERTINFO COMMAND


Generate certificate information in xml file for the given hex file.

Below is the syntax :
          CERTINFO -inputfile [input hex file name] -mode [bigendian or littleendian] -hsm_file [HSM xml configuration file] -hsm_config [true or false to enable HSM configuration handling] -output [output xml file name] -infoblockaddr [infoblock start address]       

----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES              |    DESCRIPTION																	
----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -inputfile         |    Input hex file name. 																										
   -mode           	  |    Mode type eg. bigendian or littleendian.												
   -hsm_file   		  |    HSM configuration xml file name.																
   -hsm_config        |    true or false to enable HSM configuration handling.	
   -infoblockaddress  |    Infoblock start address.		
   -output            |    Output xml file name.   													   
----------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:
	1)	CERTINFO -inputfile MG1CS080_02_40P_T0A00_HSM2.hex -mode LittleEndian -infoblockaddr 0x80000020 -output signInfo.xml
	
	2)  CERTINFO -inputfile HSM.hex -mode LittleEndian -hsm_file merged_corecfg_export.xml -hsm_config true -output signInfo.xml
